===Etymology 2===
From {{suffix|en|gum|gloss1=(substance)|y}}. The noun was influenced by {{m|en|gummi}} (from {{cog|de|-}}).

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er}}

# Resembling gum {{gloss|the substance}}.
# Covered with gum or a substance resembling gum.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=9|passage=the '''gummie''' bark of Firr or Pine|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Juvenal Satires|3|passage=Then rubs his '''gummy''' eyes.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|slang}} {{cap|thick}}; [[fat]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1857|author=Charles Waterton|title=Essays on Natural History: 3d Series|page=202
|passage=Probably, in times gone by, when flowing gowns were seldom worn in England, some fashionable dame of high degree, having splay feet, or '''gummy''' ankles, might have put them under cover.}}

